# DO NOT DELETE.
# This marker keeps the backend/data directory present in the git repository.
# Without it a fresh clone has no backend/data folder, and when that folder is
# used as a Docker bind-mount Docker (running as root) auto-creates it as
# root:root, which shows a red "locked / read-only" icon and blocks users from
# creating/renaming/deleting files. With this marker present, the folder is
# checked out owned by the cloning user and stays writable.
